❯ Upgrade blue's observation and actor so it can reason about mobile and        
  airborne threats over time without receiving hidden ground truth.             
                                                                                
  Requirements:                                                                 
  1. Include sensed vertical velocity for airborne threats; do not hard-code vz 
  to zero.                                                                      
  2. Add observable relative closure, track age/confidence, and                 
  last-known-track uncertainty.                                                 
  3. Replace nearest-only K-threat selection with a deterministic union of      
  nearest sensed threats and highest observable-risk threats. Do not rank using 
  information unavailable to blue.                                              
  4. Add a recurrent actor option, preferably a GRU after the set encoders.     
  Carry and reset per-agent hidden state through training, evaluation, replay,  
  respawn, checkpointing, and resume.                                           
  5. Preserve a feed-forward compatibility mode for old checkpoints, with       
  explicit schema/version checks.                                               
  6. Test masking, permutation invariance, hidden-state reset, temporary        
  terrain masking, JIT/VMAP, and the actor's continued lack of centralized      
  state.                                                                        
  7. Add an ablation protocol comparing feed-forward and recurrent policies on  
  mobile-ground and airborne-interceptor scenario families.                     

